# Shadow Boxing Workout App — Teardown & PunchPal AI Coach Adaptation Plan

**Version 5** — major rewrite of §5 and adds §6 + §7. Supersedes v4. Key design changes from v4:

- **Both modes now embed defense/footwork inside the combo notation**, scaled by tier (Beginner: none, Intermediate: light, Advanced: heavy). The two modes differ in *delivery cadence and coaching presence*, not in combo content.
- **Classic = teaching mode.** Bell + immediate combo at t=0, long-form description (~10–12s) at t=4–5, then Claude-decided form-only reminders distributed across the remaining ~155s, scaled to combo complexity (2–3 / 3–5 / 4–6 reminders by tier).
- **Dynamic = drilling mode.** Bell + immediate combo at t=0, no intro speech, no fillers, combos rotate at Shadow Boxing-matched cadence (Beginner 25s / Intermediate 17s / Advanced 12s) until end-of-round bell warning at t=170.
- **Combo notation extends to support inline defense/footwork tokens** like `1-2-slip_right-3-pivot`. Spec in new §7.
- **Full rating-driven within-level progression** (Just Right +10 / Too Easy +15 / Too Hard +5 / Early Exit +2 / Skipped +8). At progress=100, celebration modal prompts user to advance — they can Stay (re-prompt after 3 more "Too Easy" ratings) or Advance. Demotion safety net via Profile hint if 3+ of last 5 ratings post-advancement are Too Hard. Cap-state variety signal sent to Claude when user is Staying at progress=100. Spec in new §6.
- Removed v4's "cadence as lead time" framing — turned out to feel like dead silence in practice rather than coaching presence. Both modes now run tight cadences with real coaching content.

**Version 4** — Anchor + Variations model, wider beginner cadence as "lead time" mechanic, pre-warning concept rejected, segmented control on Home for mode switching. Superseded.

**Version 3** — pre-warning approach for cognitive lead time. Rejected because spoken pre-warnings felt naggy. Superseded.

> **Naming note (post-v4):** The "Anchor + Variations" / "Pad Work" model used in Shadow Boxing's teardown (§1–§4) ships in PunchPal as the **Dynamic** mode on the Home screen. We renamed it because user testing showed "Pad Work" makes non-boxers assume they need physical pads or a partner.

## TL;DR

- **Shadow Boxing Workout App** (Marc Gauthier / EZ-Lab Studio, App Store ID 1510911574) is the dominant solo-shadow-boxing iOS app: **4.9★ from 2.7K ratings**, **145K+ cumulative downloads**, free with a paid tier (~£15/yr). Uses **Apple system TTS**, calls punches **by number** using the same 1-jab / 2-cross / 3-lead-hook / 4-rear-hook / 5-lead-uppercut / 6-rear-uppercut convention PunchPal already uses. The "Pad Work" mode rotates combos within a round at qualitatively "steady" (beginner) to "faster" (advanced) cadence.
- **PunchPal's adaptation ships as two distinct modes** rather than one. **Classic** (teaching) gets the full description + form reminders distributed through the round. **Dynamic** (drilling) gets pad-work cadence with no fillers. **Both** modes share embedded defense/footwork inside the combo notation, scaled by tier.
- **Within-level progression** is rating-driven and automatic. Cross-level advancement requires user agency (celebration modal with Stay / Advance choice, with sensible re-prompt + demotion safety nets). The 9-tier system already in the codebase becomes a fine-grained difficulty knob inside each level rather than the primary progression mechanic.

